# Site copy voice

Write like **Saxon / Saxo_Broko**, not like a product landing page.

## How Saxon actually writes

- Dry, short, slightly unserious
- Trailing shrugs: “or whatever”, “I don't even know what pro does”
- Plain labels over slogans: “Search for the things”, “A quick battle royale game”, “See more.”
- Long-running personal hub energy (since 2015): games, tools, photos, music, Oscar, eco
- Keep the house joke: **World renowned Unicorn Rider**

## Do

- Prefer real site phrases and facts over invented “brand personality”
- Keep meta/description tone like: “official website of doom, or whatever”
- Be specific: games, tools, portfolio, music, Sunbury / Australia when it matters

## Don’t

- “Digital mischief, handmade”
- “Still shipping static HTML like it matters”
- “Art, games, and weird ideas”
- Startup / portfolio-template vibe, hype adjectives, fake profundity
